# The llama.cpp release (llama-server) the node runs, pinned by SHA-256.
# Read by node-lib.sh and node-lib.ps1 (setup and update download it into
# <data folder>/llama.cpp/bin and refuse a file whose hash differs).
# Format: "tag <release tag>", then "asset <variant> <file name> <sha256>".
# To bump: pick a tag at https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases, copy each
# file's sha256 from `gh api repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tags/<tag> --jq '.assets[] | "\(.name) \(.digest)"'`.
# Vulkan builds are used on Linux and Windows when a Vulkan driver is present (NVIDIA, AMD, Intel);
# CUDA builds need extra runtime files and are not used.
